@*
    OdsSubscriptionStatusChip — the read display of a subscription's lifecycle state (issue #293)
    as ONE chip: Paused (temporarily not billing, still visible), Ended (its term has lapsed —
    DERIVED from EndDate, never stored), Archived (retired and hidden), or Active.

    A subscription has exactly one lifecycle state. The states are ORDERED rather than orthogonal:
    only an ended subscription can be archived, so Archived implies Ended, and Ended makes a pause
    moot. Precedence is therefore Archived → Ended → Paused → Active, and this renders the first
    that applies (Active only when ShowActive). Superseded timestamps are not lost — the record body
    carries a tile per stored flag (paused / archived), which is where the full history lives.

    Sibling of OdsCoverageStatusChip / OdsContractStatusChip: the state meaning lives in the visible
    text label, never colour or glyph alone (the leading dot/icon is aria-hidden). Tone follows the
    finance vocabulary — Paused = pending (amber), Ended = expense (coral), Archived = neutral,
    Active = active (mint).
*@

@if (State is { } state)
{
    <span class="odc-substatus">
        <OdsChip Tone="state.Tone" Icon="@(ShowIcon ? state.Icon : null)" Dot="@(!ShowIcon)">@state.Label</OdsChip>
    </span>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Whether the subscription is currently paused. Ignored when <see cref="Ended"/> or
    /// <see cref="Archived"/> is set — both supersede it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Paused { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the subscription's term has lapsed (derived: EndDate ≤ today). Supersedes
    /// Paused; superseded by Archived.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Ended { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the subscription is archived. Only an ended subscription can be archived,
    /// so this supersedes every other state.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Archived { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Render an "Active" chip when no state is set (default false — a plain active row
    /// shows nothing).</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool ShowActive { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Lead the chip with its glyph instead of a dot.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool ShowIcon { get; set; }

    private sealed record SubscriptionState(string Label, OdsChipTone Tone, string Icon);

    /// <summary>Exactly one state, by precedence: Archived → Ended → Paused → Active.</summary>
    private SubscriptionState? State =>
        Archived ? new("Archived", OdsChipTone.Outline, "inventory_2")
        : Ended ? new("Ended", OdsChipTone.Expense, "event_busy")
        : Paused ? new("Paused", OdsChipTone.Pending, "pause_circle")
        : ShowActive ? new("Active", OdsChipTone.Income, "autorenew")
        : null;
}
